Package: snbr
Type: Package
Title: Bias Reduction in Skew-Normal Regression
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Enio A. C.", "Lopes", role = "aut"),
    person("Klaus L. P.", "Vasconcellos", role = "aut"),
    person("Raydonal", "Ospina", email = "raydonal@castlab.org", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Maximum likelihood, corrective (Cox and Snell) and preventive
    (mean and median bias-reducing adjusted score) estimation for linear and
    partially linear regression models with skew-normal errors. Infinite
    estimates of the shape parameter are detected exactly, the second-order
    bias is computed from exact cumulants of the log-likelihood derivatives,
    and the nonparametric component is represented by penalized B-splines.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: stats, quadprog, splines
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), knitr, rmarkdown, sn
Config/testthat/edition: 3
VignetteBuilder: knitr
LazyData: true
URL: https://raydonal.github.io/snbr/
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
